# Command glances

## What does this command do:

Glances an Eye on your system. A top/htop alternative for GNU/Linux, BSD, Mac OS and Windows operating systems.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: sudo dnf install glances
For Raspberry Pi install using: sudo apt install glances
For Mac install using: brew install glances

## Command path

For Fedora run: /usr/bin/glances
For Raspberry Pi run: /usr/bin/glances
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/glances

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/nicolargo/glances

## Command options

# Launch standalone TUI (most common usage)
glances

# Web server mode — exposes TUI at http://localhost:61208/ and REST API
glances -w

# REST API only (no web UI)
glances -w --disable-webui

# Per-CPU mode (one row per core)
glances -1

# Light mode (top menu only)
glances --light

# Set refresh interval (default 2s)
glances -t 5

# Filter processes by name/regex
glances -f nginx

# Sort process list
glances --sort-processes cpu_percent     # also: memory_percent, username, cpu_times, io_counters, name

# Accumulate processes by program name
glances --programs

# Server mode (XML-RPC, port 61209)
glances -s

# Client mode — connect to a Glances server
glances -c <ip_or_hostname>

# TUI browser (discover Glances servers on LAN)
glances --browser

# WebUI central browser
glances --browser -w

# Export stats to CSV
glances --export csv --export-csv-file /tmp/glances.csv

# Export stats to JSON file
glances --export-json-file /tmp/glances.json

# Print stats to stdout (one stat per line)
glances --stdout cpu.user,mem.used,load

# Print stats as JSON to stdout
glances --stdout-json cpu,mem,load

# Print stats as CSV to stdout
glances --stdout-csv cpu.user,mem.used,load

# List all available modules (plugins + exporters)
glances --modules-list

# Enable a disabled plugin (e.g. sensors, irq)
glances --enable-plugin sensors

# Disable specific plugins
glances --disable-plugin network,ports

# Disable all plugins except chosen ones
glances --disable-plugin all --enable-plugin cpu,mem,load

# Show temperatures in Fahrenheit
glances --fahrenheit

# Display network rate in bytes/s (default: bits/s)
glances -b

# Use a custom config file
glances -C ~/.config/glances/glances.conf

# Display field descriptions (API doc)
glances --api-doc

# Run self-test of all plugins
glances --issue

# Disable kernel threads in process list
glances --hide-kernel-threads

# Sparkline graphs in curses UI
glances --sparkline
